- That makes a lot of sense.
- Seriously.

462
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:13,915
I mean it. Really.

463
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:16,501
I mean, there was
only one person who flunked.

464
00:22:16,585 --> 00:22:17,627
Seriously.

465
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:23,133
- Your first impressions?
- What, like when I first arrived?

466
00:22:23,216 --> 00:22:25,385
I thought there were
a lot of arrogant guys.

467
00:22:25,469 --> 00:22:26,511
Yeah, I get you.

468
00:22:26,595 --> 00:22:29,139
- Like, that guy with a tattoo on his face?
- Oh, yeah.

469
00:22:29,222 --> 00:22:31,266
So, I was like, "Damn,
that's so intimidating."

470
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:35,395
But, like, even though he has tattoos
and was acting cocky, he didn't talk.

471
00:22:35,479 --> 00:22:38,106
- I know, right?
- Like when we were all eating.

472
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:40,609
But he's totally different
when it's just the two of us.

473
00:22:40,692 --> 00:22:41,777
Guess that's normal.

474
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:44,196
- When it's the two of us, he talks a lot.
- Mmm.

475
00:22:44,279 --> 00:22:47,324
I kind of thought he was tired
from his first romance.

476
00:22:47,407 --> 00:22:49,826
I was like, "Come on,
show us you're a man."

477
00:22:50,369 --> 00:22:52,913
- Right? Like, you gotta fight.
- Yeah.

478
00:22:52,996 --> 00:22:54,456
He knows what happened last time,

479
00:22:54,956 --> 00:22:58,210
so I wanted him to be the kind of guy
who'd be like, "Okay, let's go," you know?

480
00:22:58,293 --> 00:23:01,797
- For him to take the lead.
- Yeah. Kind of pathetic, right?

481
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:05,342
Hey, don't talk shit about Tai-chan.
You literally just met him!

482
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:10,013
Tai-chan's already getting
really harshly criticized by the women.

483
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:12,891
But we already know
from having watched the first group…

484
00:23:12,974 --> 00:23:15,102
- Yeah.
- …somebody will definitely like him.

485
00:23:15,185 --> 00:23:16,937
- Who likes Tai-chan?
- No, you know what?

486
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:18,730
I think that they all like Tai-chan.

487
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:21,566
- Yeah, they're definitely interested.
- Okay, I see.

488
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:24,152
I mean, they're always talking
about Tai-chan.

489
00:23:24,236 --> 00:23:25,529
- True.
- All of them.

490
00:23:26,154 --> 00:23:29,157
If they didn't like him,
they wouldn't talk about him. I see.

491
00:23:29,241 --> 00:23:32,202
I mean, if I was a girl,
I would go for Tai-chan.

492
00:23:37,916 --> 00:23:39,584
- Here it is.
- What is it?

493
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,339
<i>You are now going to write a love letter,</i>

494
00:23:44,423 --> 00:23:47,092
<i>to one person here</i>
<i>that you're interested in.</i>

495
00:23:47,175 --> 00:23:48,385
Just one?

496
00:23:48,468 --> 00:23:50,303
Yay!

497
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:52,431
- What do I do?
- Mmm…

498
00:23:52,514 --> 00:23:54,641
<i>Write an anonymous love letter</i>

499
00:23:54,724 --> 00:23:57,686
<i>to a person that you met</i>
<i>who you have feelings for.</i>

500
00:23:57,769 --> 00:23:58,728
Oh, anonymous.

501
00:23:58,812 --> 00:24:03,066
<i>Please put your letters</i>
<i>in the mailbox outside</i>, <i>one by one.</i>

502
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:12,159
WE HAVEN'T TALKED MUCH…
I'D LIKE TO TALK MORE…

503
00:24:14,578 --> 00:24:17,122
- <i>Who's Tai-chan writing to?</i>
<i>- Who, who, who?</i>

504
00:24:22,836 --> 00:24:23,795
SHARAN

505
00:24:23,879 --> 00:24:26,798
- <i>Okay, I see!</i>
- <i>Ohh!</i>

506
00:24:30,260 --> 00:24:33,263
Sharan. She has a really pretty face.

507
00:24:36,933 --> 00:24:37,893
This is it.

508
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:45,192
TAI-CHAN

509
00:24:45,275 --> 00:24:47,068
<i>All right!</i>

510
00:24:47,152 --> 00:24:49,279
<i>I put my love letter</i>
<i>in Tai-chan's mailbox.</i>

511
00:24:49,362 --> 00:24:52,949
<i>We're the same age,</i>
<i>and he's really easy to talk to.</i>

512
00:24:53,742 --> 00:24:55,076
And he's really kind.

513
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,745
I'm curious about him.

514
00:25:02,792 --> 00:25:03,627
Okay.

515
00:25:04,503 --> 00:25:05,962
I sent my letter to Maru.

516
00:25:06,963 --> 00:25:10,425
<i>He said to me, "I don't usually cook,</i>
<i>so could you please teach me?"</i>

517
00:25:10,509 --> 00:25:12,636
I thought that was cute. Mmm.

518
00:25:15,430 --> 00:25:17,182
I'm embarrassed.

519
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:21,019
<i>- Oh, it's the…</i>
<i>- It's the keeper.</i>

520
00:25:21,102 --> 00:25:22,812
- <i>Ryopi the keeper.</i>
- <i>Yeah.</i>

521
00:25:22,896 --> 00:25:27,192
He livens up the mood the most,
and it's fun talking to him.

522
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:32,155
A girl…

523
00:25:37,285 --> 00:25:38,537
RINRIN

524
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:40,664
<i>Huh, there are already couples here.</i>

525
00:25:40,747 --> 00:25:43,750
- <i>Yeah, they look good together.</i>
- <i>They have the same vibe.</i>

526
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:51,383
<i>Kazuma's giving his to her, right?</i>

527
00:25:52,342 --> 00:25:54,803
<i>He's given his letter to Sara,</i>
<i>with the tattoo.</i>

528
00:25:54,886 --> 00:25:55,971
<i>From Okinawa.</i>

529
00:25:59,224 --> 00:26:01,810
- <i>Who could it be?</i>
- <i>Oh, remember the tomatoes?</i>

530
00:26:01,893 --> 00:26:03,019
<i>Right, yeah.</i>

531
00:26:03,103 --> 00:26:04,813
SARA

532
00:26:33,883 --> 00:26:35,552
<i>Good morning, everyone.</i>

533
00:26:35,635 --> 00:26:38,388
<i>You will now go</i>
<i>to your mailbox one by one,</i>

534
00:26:38,972 --> 00:26:41,308
<i>and check to see</i>
<i>if you have a love letter.</i>

535
00:26:42,684 --> 00:26:43,685
It won't be zero.

536
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:47,606
- Yeah, no way for me either.
- I feel confident about that.

537
00:26:48,356 --> 00:26:49,482
What if it is zero?

538
00:26:50,108 --> 00:26:52,402
- I'll jump in the sea.
- It's too early, bro.

539
00:26:52,485 --> 00:26:54,904
It's raining.

540
00:26:55,864 --> 00:26:58,116
That doesn't matter. It's for the feeling.

541
00:26:59,242 --> 00:27:02,454
But, hey, Kazuma has
quite a pretty face, doesn't he?

542
00:27:02,537 --> 00:27:04,456
Yeah. I think he's cute.

543
00:27:04,539 --> 00:27:05,832
He's always smiling.

544
00:27:05,915 --> 00:27:07,208
- I know!
- He's cheeky.

545
00:27:07,292 --> 00:27:09,044
- He is.
- Yeah, he's really cheeky.

546
00:27:09,544 --> 00:27:12,213
- So how should we announce it?
- Yeah.

547
00:27:13,131 --> 00:27:14,466
Should we all show ours at once?

548
00:27:14,549 --> 00:27:16,384
- At once?
- Let's do that.

549
00:27:16,468 --> 00:27:18,303
But I don't want to see what's inside.

550
00:27:18,386 --> 00:27:19,554
Yeah, we can hide that.

551
00:27:20,930 --> 00:27:23,600
So you just do this
with your hand if you got zero.

552
00:27:24,809 --> 00:27:25,685
All right.

553
00:27:26,269 --> 00:27:27,771
Well, I guess I'll go first.

554
00:27:27,854 --> 00:27:30,231
- Hope it goes well.
- You're getting zero.

555
00:27:30,315 --> 00:27:33,777
I know I'm not getting zero.
I'm gonna come back with four.

556
00:27:35,403 --> 00:27:36,404
All right.

557
00:27:57,008 --> 00:27:58,134
Thanks.

558
00:28:02,722 --> 00:28:04,557
- He's already back.
- Oh, he's here.

559
00:28:04,641 --> 00:28:07,227
- How does he look?
- Yeah, he's grinning.

560
00:28:07,894 --> 00:28:08,812
He is.

561
00:28:10,188 --> 00:28:12,482
You got zero, right?
Your face says it all.

562
00:28:14,401 --> 00:28:16,027
What is that?

563
00:28:16,111 --> 00:28:17,862
So annoying.

564
00:28:17,946 --> 00:28:19,906
- What's that mean?
- So damn annoying.

565
00:28:26,871 --> 00:28:27,747
Nice

566
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:31,292
Nice.

567
00:28:32,836 --> 00:28:33,795
Not zero.

568
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:35,505
Okay.

569
00:28:39,843 --> 00:28:40,802
Hmm.

570
00:28:42,137 --> 00:28:44,305
Damn, I thought there would be two.

571
00:28:46,224 --> 00:28:49,018
- I hate how this feels.
- I know. And it's so hot.

572
00:28:49,102 --> 00:28:51,187
- I want air conditioning.
- Right?

573
00:28:57,527 --> 00:28:59,571
<i>Hmm, I wonder if he has any.</i>

574
00:29:00,822 --> 00:29:01,781
<i>Ohh!</i>

575
00:29:04,659 --> 00:29:05,660
I chose Rune.

576
00:29:07,036 --> 00:29:09,164
We think the same way,

577
00:29:09,247 --> 00:29:12,000
and, you know, we're both
pretty considerate of others.

578
00:29:12,584 --> 00:29:14,627
So I thought we'd get along well.

579
00:29:14,711 --> 00:29:17,338
Out of everyone here,
he's someone I'd really like

580
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:19,340
to get to know and talk to more.

581
00:29:21,468 --> 00:29:22,552
- All right.
- Come on.

582
00:29:22,635 --> 00:29:24,512
- He's going for it.
- Go for it.

583
00:29:24,596 --> 00:29:27,182
No way it's zero.
Just bring the whole mailbox.

584
00:29:29,726 --> 00:29:30,602
Give it a roar.

585
00:29:33,646 --> 00:29:35,732
<i>He said he'd jump</i>
<i>in the sea if he got zero.</i>

586
00:29:35,815 --> 00:29:36,858
<i>He did say that.</i>

587
00:29:38,443 --> 00:29:39,277
<i>Oh!</i>

588
00:29:40,779 --> 00:29:42,614
<i>His face is scary again.</i>

589
00:29:50,830 --> 00:29:51,873
It's increasing.

590
00:29:54,417 --> 00:29:56,795
- Well, well, well, well.
- Huh?

591
00:29:57,545 --> 00:29:59,255
- Well, well, well, well.
- Have one?

592
00:30:00,381 --> 00:30:01,549
- You get one?
- Uh…

593
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:02,550
I can't tell.

594
00:30:03,593 --> 00:30:05,470
- Huh?
- Huh?

595
00:30:05,553 --> 00:30:07,388
- Huh?
- Huh?

596
00:30:10,266 --> 00:30:11,893
He's fine, he's fine.

597
00:30:13,645 --> 00:30:14,479
Hmm.

598
00:30:14,979 --> 00:30:15,980
Should we do it on three?

599
00:30:16,064 --> 00:30:16,981
- On three?
- Yeah.

600
00:30:17,065 --> 00:30:18,399
Then, shall we?

601
00:30:18,483 --> 00:30:20,151
- Here we go.
- Okay.

602
00:30:20,235 --> 00:30:22,278
- This is bad.
- One, two, three.

603
00:30:24,030 --> 00:30:25,865
- Whoa.
- Wait, we each got one?

604
00:30:25,949 --> 00:30:26,825
They split them up?

605
00:30:26,908 --> 00:30:28,284
- Ta-da!
- One each.

606
00:30:28,368 --> 00:30:31,955
- Oh, damn it, am I the only one?
- Okay, okay, okay.

607
00:30:32,038 --> 00:30:34,290
- You're the only one, huh?
- Are you serious?

608
00:30:34,374 --> 00:30:36,125
I'm pissed I lost to this guy. Dang.

609
00:30:36,209 --> 00:30:38,545
YOU'RE THE ONE I'M INTERESTED IN.
I'D LIKE TO TALK AGAIN.

610
00:30:38,628 --> 00:30:40,922
I wonder who this is.
Her handwriting's pretty.

611
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:44,467
They're not signed.

612
00:30:44,551 --> 00:30:46,386
YOU'RE THE ONE
I WANT TO GET TO KNOW THE MOST.

613
00:30:48,054 --> 00:30:49,681
TO MARU, I HAD FUN MAKING CURRY WITH YOU

614
00:30:49,764 --> 00:30:51,182
I'D BE HAPPY IF WE COULD TALK MORE!

615
00:30:52,934 --> 00:30:55,019
THANKS FOR TODAY! WE'RE THE SAME AGE…

616
00:30:55,103 --> 00:30:58,273
Is it seriously just me?
I'm damn pissed. Like, seriously?

617
00:31:01,484 --> 00:31:02,944
Zero letters is tough.

618
00:31:04,112 --> 00:31:06,030
I'm the only loser.

619
00:31:07,574 --> 00:31:09,325
I'm surprised it was so even.

620
00:31:10,076 --> 00:31:11,202
- Yeah, me too.
- Yeah.

621
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:14,122
I'm gonna go, I'm getting super pissed.

622
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:18,084
- You're really going?
- To the sea? Yeah.

623
00:31:18,167 --> 00:31:19,627
- Awesome!
- I'm a man.

624
00:31:21,462 --> 00:31:23,464
- Go for it, Kazuma!
- Be careful though.

625
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:25,884
- You just watch!
- <i>Everyone's cheering him on.</i>

626
00:31:25,967 --> 00:31:27,260
<i>- So cute.</i>
- <i>It's cute.</i>

627
00:31:27,844 --> 00:31:29,637
I am a man!

628
00:31:29,721 --> 00:31:31,347
Go for it, bro.

629
00:31:33,224 --> 00:31:37,270
<i>That was way too shallow.</i>
<i>I wanted him to jump in somewhere deep.</i>

630
00:31:37,353 --> 00:31:39,063
- Nice job.
- Awesome, bro!

631
00:31:39,147 --> 00:31:41,649
That was beautiful to watch.

632
00:31:41,733 --> 00:31:44,110
- It was a perfect dive.
- Yeah, super beautiful.

633
00:31:44,193 --> 00:31:46,404
There was no splash at all.

634
00:31:47,572 --> 00:31:50,658
I'll show you what it means to be a man!

635
00:31:51,242 --> 00:31:52,535
Well said!

636
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:54,829
Leave it to me!

637
00:31:56,998 --> 00:31:58,041
You think you'll get any?

638
00:31:58,541 --> 00:32:01,210
- I want one from the person I wrote to.
- Yeah, I want that too.

639
00:32:01,294 --> 00:32:03,129
- Of course.
- For sure, yeah.

640
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:07,342
Wow, I'm nervous.

641
00:32:17,685 --> 00:32:20,939
- Hey, I'm back.
- Welcome back. How many do you have?

642
00:32:21,022 --> 00:32:23,358
I got two letters.

643
00:32:23,441 --> 00:32:26,444
Wait, but I haven't opened them yet.
This one is really long.

644
00:32:26,527 --> 00:32:28,821
You can see through it.

645
00:32:30,782 --> 00:32:31,908
"To Sharan.

646
00:32:31,991 --> 00:32:35,620
I really enjoyed talking to you
so much today. Thank you."

647
00:32:35,703 --> 00:32:39,332
- Oh, I've figured it out. It's Tai-chan.
- Oh, it's from Tai-chan?

648
00:32:39,415 --> 00:32:42,251
"I want to get to know you
better. Let's keep on talking."

649
00:32:42,335 --> 00:32:45,088
Hey, what do you think about
him having face tattoos?

650
00:32:45,171 --> 00:32:47,840
- It's stylish, I like it.
- Because it's stylish? Hmm.

651
00:32:47,924 --> 00:32:50,593
- Did you ask him why he got them?
- I didn't ask.

652
00:32:51,177 --> 00:32:52,929
- I'm curious.
- Then who's this one from?

653
00:32:53,012 --> 00:32:54,847
- Who's this from?
- I don't know!

654
00:32:55,390 --> 00:32:57,350
"We have a lot in common,
so it's easy to…"

655
00:32:57,433 --> 00:32:59,769
Oh, wait. I think I know.

656
00:32:59,852 --> 00:33:00,979
It might be Maru.

657
00:33:01,062 --> 00:33:03,648
Oh! Really?

658
00:33:03,731 --> 00:33:05,024
You wrote yours to Maru, right?

659
00:33:05,108 --> 00:33:06,025
- I did.
- Thought so.

660
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:17,328
<i>Aw.</i>

661
00:33:18,621 --> 00:33:19,914
- I'm upset.
- Huh?

662
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:21,165
I didn't get a letter.

663
00:33:21,249 --> 00:33:22,166
- Really?
- What?

664
00:33:22,250 --> 00:33:23,167
- Yeah.
- No way!

665
00:33:23,251 --> 00:33:25,420
- I feel so sad.
- Wait, who did you talk to?

666
00:33:25,503 --> 00:33:26,587
- So, uh…
- Maru?

667
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:27,880
Uh, yeah, that's right.

668
00:33:27,964 --> 00:33:29,090
I mostly talked to Maru.

669
00:33:29,173 --> 00:33:31,300
- No way
- Then it can't be helped.

670
00:33:31,384 --> 00:33:33,052
- It's just the start.
- Guess you're right.

671
00:33:33,136 --> 00:33:36,055
- Yeah, stay positive.
- Right, we haven't talked to everyone.

672
00:33:36,139 --> 00:33:38,266
We can make up
for it starting this morning.

673
00:33:38,349 --> 00:33:40,560
- That's what a strong woman does.
- Hmm, yeah.

674
00:33:55,074 --> 00:33:57,201
- She got one?
- Yeah, she does.

675
00:33:57,285 --> 00:33:58,119
I'm back.

676
00:33:58,202 --> 00:33:59,537
- Welcome back.
- Hey, girl.

677
00:34:00,163 --> 00:34:01,539
- Huh?
- Two?

678
00:34:02,540 --> 00:34:04,709
She got two! Oh, no!

679
00:34:04,792 --> 00:34:06,544
No way!

680
00:34:06,627 --> 00:34:08,296
- Oh, that's good.
- I can't see through it.

681
00:34:08,379 --> 00:34:09,881
This one's only one line long.

682
00:34:09,964 --> 00:34:12,383
- Uh, who's it from?
- Oh, I know. I know who.

683
00:34:12,467 --> 00:34:14,427
- It looks like Kazuma.
- It does.

684
00:34:14,510 --> 00:34:16,012
- I'm opening Kazuma's.
- Okay.

685
00:34:16,095 --> 00:34:17,764
- "Sara…"
- Oh?

686
00:34:17,847 --> 00:34:20,558
"We didn't get to talk much,
but I'd like to talk more."

687
00:34:20,641 --> 00:34:24,062
Yeah, I think it's Kazuma.
I only talked about tattoos with Kazuma.

688
00:34:24,145 --> 00:34:25,646
- That's what he means.
- Hmm.

689
00:34:26,230 --> 00:34:27,398
- I'm opening it.
- Okay.

690
00:34:28,775 --> 00:34:29,692
Oh, crap.

691
00:34:29,776 --> 00:34:33,362
"Thanks for eating my tomatoes.
Let's drink some wine together soon."

692
00:34:33,446 --> 00:34:34,864
Rune!

693
00:34:34,947 --> 00:34:36,491
- Rune.
- It's Rune!

694
00:34:36,574 --> 00:34:37,992
- So I've got Ryopi's?
- Yeah.

695
00:34:38,076 --> 00:34:39,911
- Definitely.
- That's right.

696
00:34:48,628 --> 00:34:50,546
- I'm back.
- Welcome back.

697
00:34:50,630 --> 00:34:52,048
- So you got one then?
- I did.

698
