931
00:44:46,266 --> 00:44:49,395
So this was the first time since then--
No, it was the first time in my life.

932
00:44:49,478 --> 00:44:51,146
- That makes me happy.
- Does it?

933
00:44:51,230 --> 00:44:53,440
- How come you started rapping?
- Rapping?

934
00:44:53,524 --> 00:44:57,736
Well, the thing is,
I always wanted to be a real hero.

935
00:44:57,820 --> 00:45:00,364
What? What do you mean? Like a superhero?

936
00:45:00,447 --> 00:45:02,616
Yeah, exactly.
I always wanted to be a hero.

937
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:03,784
Right.

938
00:45:04,368 --> 00:45:07,871
I entered the Junon Superboy Contest,
thinking it would make me a hero.

939
00:45:07,955 --> 00:45:09,164
- Really?
- I was accepted.

940
00:45:09,248 --> 00:45:10,249
Wow.

941
00:45:10,332 --> 00:45:12,668
And I was chosen
as the 25th Junon Superboy.

942
00:45:12,751 --> 00:45:13,752
Mmm.

943
00:45:13,836 --> 00:45:17,423
And about a year and a half later,
I became a Kamen Rider.

944
00:45:17,506 --> 00:45:19,842
What? A Kamen Rider? What do you mean?

945
00:45:19,925 --> 00:45:21,593
- A Kamen Rider.
- Wearing the suit?

946
00:45:21,677 --> 00:45:23,303
Not the guy inside the suit.

947
00:45:23,387 --> 00:45:25,472
I was in the <i>Kamen Rider </i>show
for about a year.

948
00:45:25,556 --> 00:45:27,391
- You became a Kamen Rider?
- Yeah.

949
00:45:27,474 --> 00:45:28,767
- And--
- That's crazy!

950
00:45:28,851 --> 00:45:30,602
- Yeah.
- Oh my god. That's so funny!

951
00:45:30,686 --> 00:45:34,314
Yeah. So, I got a lot of other acting jobs
off of the back of that.

952
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:36,692
But I had always wanted to be
a Kamen Rider,

953
00:45:36,775 --> 00:45:39,611
so I felt like I had accomplished my goal,

954
00:45:39,695 --> 00:45:41,739
- and I was burned out.
- You felt satisfied? I see.

955
00:45:41,822 --> 00:45:43,866
- I felt like I was missing something.
- The opposite?

956
00:45:43,949 --> 00:45:45,367
- There was a hole in my heart.
- Oh.

957
00:45:45,451 --> 00:45:47,911
Yeah. And rap was
what filled that hole for me.

958
00:45:47,995 --> 00:45:49,788
- Oh, that's amazing.
- Yeah.

959
00:45:49,872 --> 00:45:51,123
- It's interesting.
- Yeah.

960
00:45:57,379 --> 00:45:58,922
It's starting to piss me off.

961
00:46:04,178 --> 00:46:06,889
So, do you, like,
wanna be a famous rapper?

962
00:46:07,931 --> 00:46:10,726
That's my number one goal. With rapping.

963
00:46:11,769 --> 00:46:13,312
What, so you wanna go global?

964
00:46:14,688 --> 00:46:17,274
Mmm, yeah, I want to go global, but…

965
00:46:19,193 --> 00:46:21,487
- So a little while ago, my…
- Mmm.

966
00:46:22,404 --> 00:46:24,907
…my mother got cancer.

967
00:46:24,990 --> 00:46:26,366
- For real?
- Yeah.

968
00:46:26,450 --> 00:46:27,576
- No way.
- Yeah.

969
00:46:27,659 --> 00:46:28,744
So…

970
00:46:28,827 --> 00:46:30,245
- Way back then,
- Hmm.

971
00:46:30,329 --> 00:46:32,748
I would go into the studio,
like, all the time,

972
00:46:32,831 --> 00:46:35,125
- Hmm.
- 'cause I was always making songs.

973
00:46:35,209 --> 00:46:37,878
- I didn't spend much time with my family.
- Mmm, yeah.

974
00:46:38,462 --> 00:46:40,714
And so, then I… I guess I realized,

975
00:46:40,798 --> 00:46:43,300
that I should spend more time
with my family.

976
00:46:43,383 --> 00:46:44,218
Hmm.

977
00:46:44,301 --> 00:46:46,637
So if I live my life the proper way,

978
00:46:46,720 --> 00:46:49,097
I can see them when I wake up
in the morning.

979
00:46:49,181 --> 00:46:51,809
And I can have dinner with them
when I come home.

980
00:46:51,892 --> 00:46:54,436
And then I can just do
my own thing during the day.

981
00:46:55,020 --> 00:46:57,189
And when I had my first live performance,

982
00:46:57,272 --> 00:47:00,442
it was at a really small venue,
but she was still able to come.

983
00:47:00,526 --> 00:47:02,152
- For real?
- Yeah.

984
00:47:02,236 --> 00:47:04,112
And it was my first time performing.

985
00:47:04,196 --> 00:47:07,324
I didn't have any fans, and I didn't even
tell my friends about it.

986
00:47:07,407 --> 00:47:08,534
- Really?
- Yeah.

987
00:47:08,617 --> 00:47:10,911
It really was like
I was performing on my own.

988
00:47:11,620 --> 00:47:14,373
- Anyway, she was the only one who came.
- Oh god.

989
00:47:14,456 --> 00:47:17,251
And while everyone
was just sitting there in silence…

990
00:47:17,334 --> 00:47:19,169
I mean, it's okay, nobody knew my name,

991
00:47:19,253 --> 00:47:21,797
and my songs
weren't exactly good back then, so…

992
00:47:21,880 --> 00:47:22,798
Hmm.

993
00:47:22,881 --> 00:47:24,174
But I gave it my all.

994
00:47:24,258 --> 00:47:25,592
And she was the only one

995
00:47:26,176 --> 00:47:28,554
who was like,
"You're so cool! You're the best!"

996
00:47:28,637 --> 00:47:31,974
- Really? That's so sweet.
- She was the only one cheering me on.

997
00:47:32,057 --> 00:47:34,893
- So touching.
- And it made me so, so happy, you know?

998
00:47:34,977 --> 00:47:37,271
Oh my god. I feel so moved. It's too much.

999
00:47:37,354 --> 00:47:39,481
- Yeah.
- That's so sweet.

1000
00:47:39,565 --> 00:47:41,859
- And so, that's why…
- Hmm.

1001
00:47:41,942 --> 00:47:43,569
…I wanna make it big.

1002
00:47:43,652 --> 00:47:44,611
Hmm.

1003
00:47:44,695 --> 00:47:48,615
So she can see me perform
at a big venue sooner rather than later.

1004
00:47:48,699 --> 00:47:50,534
Oh my god. That's so sweet.

1005
00:47:50,617 --> 00:47:52,119
- Yeah.
- Wow.

1006
00:47:52,202 --> 00:47:55,289
That's my biggest goal.
Of course, I want to go global too.

1007
00:47:55,372 --> 00:47:57,457
Yeah, I get that. Of course.

1008
00:48:04,381 --> 00:48:06,008
I'm getting really pissed off.

1009
00:48:12,306 --> 00:48:14,474
- Okinawa has loads of rappers.
- Yeah.

1010
00:48:14,558 --> 00:48:15,809
Like, so many.

1011
00:48:15,893 --> 00:48:18,520
But it is still really hard
to get into the industry.

1012
00:48:24,526 --> 00:48:26,820
I don't often get
to go this deep with people.

1013
00:48:26,904 --> 00:48:28,572
- I'm so moved.
- Glad to hear it.

1014
00:48:29,740 --> 00:48:33,201
- <i>Don't do it!</i>
- <i>No, Kazuma, please don't. Jeez!</i>

1015
00:48:33,285 --> 00:48:35,454
Other people have been through
a lot of the same stuff.

1016
00:48:35,537 --> 00:48:37,956
- <i>No.</i>
- <i>It's Jason from </i>Friday the 13th!

1017
00:48:38,040 --> 00:48:40,834
<i>Seriously. He's like Jason.</i>

1018
00:48:41,418 --> 00:48:43,128
<i>Kazuma!</i>

1019
00:48:43,211 --> 00:48:45,756
- Huh?
- Oh my god. What? Jason?

1020
00:48:45,839 --> 00:48:47,257
- I'm sorry.
- Is this a horror show?

1021
00:48:47,341 --> 00:48:48,342
No.

1022
00:48:48,425 --> 00:48:50,135
Is this the one where he's alive?

1023
00:48:50,218 --> 00:48:51,511
- No.
- I know what to do.

1024
00:48:51,595 --> 00:48:53,555
Give him an electric shock.

1025
00:48:53,639 --> 00:48:57,643
No, really. Tell me, do women actually
fall for this kind of thing?

1026
00:48:57,726 --> 00:49:00,145
- I wouldn't say I don't like it.
- Well…

1027
00:49:00,228 --> 00:49:03,231
I do feel bad for Kazuma,
but Rune is way cooler,

1028
00:49:03,315 --> 00:49:05,484
in terms of looks and the way he lives.

1029
00:49:05,984 --> 00:49:08,320
That's how it is.
